# Origin offer — EV backbone (primary source)

**Subject:** 728653T - 40-44 Pakington Street St Kilda - Feasibility study on the installation of EV Chargers
**From:** Morgan Wise, Business Relationships Lead, Origin Zero / E-mobility (Morgan.Wise@originenergy.com.au), 17 Jun 2026
**Also on thread:** Tayler Jones (Origin); James Ma (Amity, strata mgr); Scott Walker; Mark Tan; Kim Sandeman; Nicholas Wood

## What Origin proposes (verbatim substance)

> To fully future-proof apartment buildings for all car spaces, Origin recommends installing an **EV charging backbone** — all of the infrastructure that ensures each resident can install an EV charger should they choose to. **The backbone is the cost to the OC**; the residents then pay the cost to install the charger at their request. The proposal attached is an **indicative cost only**; a firm quote requires a site inspection by one of Origin's installers.

> Origin typically sees resident charger installs cost around **$3,000-$6,000 ex GST after the backbone** is implemented, whereas **without** this infrastructure residents can be looking at **over $10,000 per install** (additional labour, long cable runs, conduit).

## Terms

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Scope | Building-wide EV backbone: cabling, switchboard capacity, conduit, load management. **Backbone only — no chargers.** |
