## The strongest argument (Origin's own numbers)

Declining the backbone does not save money. Origin's own figures put unaided installs at $10,000+ each vs $3,000-$6,000 with the backbone. So "saving money" by declining is an illusion — the cost just gets spent later, by individuals, in larger amounts, plus the resale/rental drag on every lot.
